I take my mobile phone and call a hair salon.
A woman answers.
“Hair salon Haarstudio, hello,” she says.
“Hello,” I say.
“I need an appointment for a haircut, please.”
“Gladly.”
“When do you have time?” asks the hairdresser.
I look at my calendar.
“Do you have time on Wednesday?” I ask.
The hairdresser checks her appointments.
“Yes, we still have appointments free on Wednesday,” she says.
“Does six o'clock suit you?”
I look at the calendar again.
I always go to the gym on Tuesday and Thursday.
But on Wednesday I have time.
“Yes, six o'clock in the evening suits perfectly,” I say.
“Very good.”
“What is your name, please?”
“Flores.”
“Maya Flores.”
“Alright, Frau Flores.”
“See you Wednesday at six o'clock!” says the hairdresser.
“Thank you very much, goodbye!” I answer.
I end the call.
